Bugfix: Enabling an outdated or previously removed app no longer breaks the instance

Enabling a disabled app whose data was older than its code only set the app to
enabled. The instance then required an upgrade until an administrator ran
`occ upgrade`, and showed the maintenance page meanwhile. Enabling now runs the
app's migrations and repair steps first.

Installing an app over tables left behind by an earlier installation stopped
with "table already exists" for apps that use database.xml. The schema is now
updated instead. During `occ upgrade`, any error while installing a new shipped
app is logged and no longer aborts the upgrade.

An app update that only raises the patch version now runs migrations that are
still missing, instead of silently skipping them on existing instances.
